commit a5aac2b52c60cc8870497b1f223d2d4967dfe0b3
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 13 08:21:11 2026 +0000

    perf(c): refuse root-token predicate ranges with no candidate token, and gate the pilot's root conditional on the ? count (#3924)
    
    The body's token prefix table gains a comma count and an assignment-operator
    count. c_ir_has_root_comma, _assignment, _control_operator, _question and
    c_ir_call_argument_separator become inline gates that answer a body range
    holding none of their candidate tokens in O(1) and keep their scans out of
    line; reference-check builds run the skipped scan. Under -fc-ast-pilot,
    c_ir_root_conditional tests the ? count before the tree's records and counts
    the refusal as the records' negative.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ9Jru6TSEK1NQeoshcsFF

